-- title:
--   Finite-type end chart with pole along the other Igusa components
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q \ge 5$ and $\ell \ge 3$ with $\ell \neq q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell \nmid M'$.
--
--   **Base field and function field.** $L$ is a field of characteristic zero, $\xi \in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and `hι` asserts the existence of a ring homomorphism $\iota \colon L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$. $K$ is an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and `hK` requires $K$ to be [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), i.e. the field generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the rational $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_H$ with $N_0 = (q\ell)^2M'$ and $H = \ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/N_0)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$.
--
--   **Arithmetic of the base ring.** $A$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain with algebraically closed residue field and fraction field $L$, equipped with an algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$; $q$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hAq`), $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), $\varpi$ generates $\mathfrak{m}_A$ (`hϖ`), and $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q \cdot u$ for a unit $u$ (`hϖt`). The element $j \in K$ is nonzero and its Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the rational $j$-series [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) (`hj`). Throughout, $C :=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` is the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, $\mathfrak{X} :=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) is the scheme obtained as the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the middle chart algebra over $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra, and `toBase` is its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   **The supersingular point.** $y$ is a maximal ideal of $C$ containing $\varpi$ (`hy`, `hϖy`), and `hss` requires: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point.
--
--   **The Drinfeld chart hypothesis `hArig`.** For every point $z$ of $\mathfrak{X}$ at which the germ of $\varpi$ (pulled back along `toBase`) lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` and satisfying the same supersingularity condition as `hss` at $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma \colon A \to W$ with $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\sigma \varpi)$, power series $f, u, v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u, v$ units and $f \equiv X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e \colon \widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathfrak{X},z} \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; S := W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})\,v - f\,u\bigr),$$
--   $\widehat{\ }$ denoting the adic completion of the stalk at its maximal ideal, subject to seven riders, summarised here: (R1) $e$ carries the germ of $a \in A$ to the class of the constant $\sigma(a)$; (R2) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) — that is, $\tau$ acts on the quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level $\Gamma_H(N_0,H)$ by the slash action of `conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`, read through any embedding $\iota$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$ — maps $C$ into $C$; (R3) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \cap \Gamma(\ell)$ such a $\tau$ restricts to the identity on $C$ modulo $y'$; (R4) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially on $C/y'$, there are an automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with: $\theta$ intertwining $e$ and the action of $\tau$ on germs of elements of $C$; $\theta$ fixing the classes of constants; $\theta(X_j) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0, X_1$; $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M_{ij} \equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$; $c \equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ if $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$; and $c \not\equiv 1$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}_W$ if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; (R5) branch separation: two primes of $S$ containing the class of $\sigma\varpi$, each omitting at least one of the classes of $X_0, X_1$, and each containing an element with linear part $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, have distinct contractions to the stalk whenever $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$; (R6) Igusa reading: for a prime $P$ of $S$ as above whose linear part may be taken to be $X_0$, an element $a \in C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$; (R7) Hasse rider: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$, lies in $C$, is congruent modulo $y'$ to the image of some $a_0 \in A$, and the germ of the difference equals the class of a power series $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0 \ge 1$ whose degree-$e_0$ binary form takes unit values at every pair $(a,b) \in W^2$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak{m}_W$.
--
--   **The fixed witness.** A point $z$ of $\mathfrak{X}$ with the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hϖz`, `hz`), a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ (`hy'`) with the supersingularity condition `hss'` and with $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal} = y$ (`hy'y`), and one chart witness $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ of exactly the shape above (`hσ₁`, `hu₁`, `hv₁`, `hf₁`) whose riders `hW₁` are the same seven clauses (R1)–(R7) for this witness.
--
--   **Centre, blow-up chart, valuation ring, other end.** The ideal $J \subseteq C$ is required (`hJ`) to be the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $\tau|_C^{-1}$ of the contraction along $e_1 \circ \mathrm{toC} \circ \mathrm{germ}_z$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$, $X_1$, taken over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. The $A$-subalgebra $B \subseteq K$ is required (`hB`) to be $C\bigl[\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}\bigr]$. $W$ is a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`), and: `hR1` states $C \subseteq B$ and that $K$ is the field of fractions of $B$; `hR2` states that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses) states that $W \cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak{m}_W = (\varpi)$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak{m}_W$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at $\mathfrak{m}_W$; `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here) states that for every $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements of $\mathfrak{m}_W$, compatible with $A \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and equivariant for the level automorphisms through an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, c)$ of [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) acting by `hAction`, with $c \neq 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \neq \mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ receives the $\mathfrak{m}_W$-part of $B$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak{m}_W$ after all such translations is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism preserving $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$. Finally, $O$ is a subring of $K$ required (`hO`) to be the localisation at some maximal ideal $P$ of the blow-up chart $C\bigl[\{x \in K : xa \in J\}\bigr]$ for some nonzero $a \in J$, such that every element of $y$ is a non-unit in $O$ and $B \not\subseteq O$; moreover $O \subseteq W$ (`hOW`), $O$ is local (`hOloc`) and noetherian (`hOnoe`), and $C \subseteq O$ (`hCO`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists an $A$-subalgebra $B_x$ of $K$ such that:
--
--   1. every element of $B_x$ lies in $B$ and in $O$;
--
--   2. $B_x$ is of finite type over $A$;
--
--   3. for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ with `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`, $\tau$ maps $B_x$ into $B_x$;
--
--   4. every $f \in B_x$ satisfies $\operatorname{ord}_P f \ge 0$ at every place $P$ of $K$ over $L$ (a valuation subring of $K$ containing $L$, different from $K$, with principal ideals) for which $\operatorname{ord}_P j \ge 0$;
--
--   5. $O$ is the localisation of $B_x$ at the elements that become units in $O$: an $f \in K$ lies in $O$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B_x$ such that $h$, whenever it lies in $O$, is a unit of $O$;
--
--   6. there is an element $b \in B_x$ with the following property: for every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ whose intersection with $L$ is exactly the image of $A$, in which $\varpi$ (if it lies in $V$) lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$, and such that $j \in V$ and no value at $j$ of a monic polynomial over $A$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_V$ when it lies in $V$, if some element of $O$ lies outside $V$ then $b \notin V$.
--
--   Thus $B_x$ is a finite-type, level-equivariant chart, contained in both $B$ and $O$, localising to $O$, whose elements are regular wherever $j$ is, and carrying a single element with a pole along every Igusa-type valuation of $K$ that does not dominate $O$.
--
--   This is a step in the local analysis at $q$ of the integral model of the modular curve of level $(q\ell)^2M'$ at a supersingular point, where the completed stalk is presented by a Drinfeld-type equation and the blow-up of the weighted centre $J$ separates the Igusa components. It produces the end-adapted affine chart of finite type, with a function having a pole along all other components, that is used by the assembly of the cyclic decomposition of the ends of the blown-up supersingular chart.
